  { q: 'Do you cover all St Helens postcodes?', a: 'Yes. We cover WA9, WA10, WA11 and WA12. That includes the town centre, Eccleston, Parr, Sutton, Thatto Heath, Haydock, Rainford, Newton-le-Willows and Earlestown. The price is the same everywhere.' },
  { q: 'My back boiler and gas fire were taken out. Does the front room radiator need to be bigger?', a: 'Usually, yes. The gas fire used to add heat to the front room. Now the radiator has to do it alone. If it was sized for a room with a fire, it will be too small. We check this when we visit.' },
  { q: 'Can you add a radiator to a room that has never had one?', a: 'Yes. Box rooms, back bedrooms and knocked-through rooms in WA10 terraces often have none. We run pipes under the floorboards or through a nearby wall. A new radiator in a new position is from £325.' },
  { q: 'Do you work for St Helens landlords?', a: 'Yes. We replace and repair radiators in rented homes across all WA postcodes. You get a fixed price, and a written record of the work for your files.' },
  { q: 'Is balancing included?', a: 'Yes, on every job. Balancing sets each radiator so the whole house heats evenly. Without it, a new radiator can starve the others of heat.' },
  { q: 'How long does it take to fit a radiator?', a: 'A straight swap takes 1 to 2 hours. A new radiator with new pipes takes 2 to 4 hours. Five radiators are usually done in one day.' },
  { q: 'How much is a radiator repair?', a: 'Repairs are charged by time. The first hour is £120 on weekdays 9am to 4pm, £150 evenings, nights and weekends, and £180 on bank holidays. There is no call-out fee.' },
  { q: 'Do I need a power flush before new radiators?', a: 'Only if the system is dirty. Signs are cold patches at the bottom of radiators and black water when you bleed them. If your radiators heat evenly, you do not need one.' },
  { q: 'Are you Gas Safe registered?', a: 'Yes. Radiator work on the heating circuit is done by our Gas Safe registered engineers. You can check any engineer on the Gas Safe Register.' },
];
