      </ul>
      <p>There is no call-out fee. A straight swap can often be priced on the phone. For new rooms and front room upgrades, we visit first. The quote visit is free, and the written price is fixed.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="back-boiler">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Why is my front room colder since the back boiler came out?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Because the gas fire has gone. It used to heat the front room as well as the radiator. Now the radiator must do the job alone, and it is often too small.</p>
      <p>Many WA10 and WA9 terraces had a back boiler behind a gas fire. Swapping it for a combi is one of the most common upgrades in St Helens. But many installers fit the same size radiator in the front room. The result is a room that is colder after the upgrade than before.</p>
      <p>We check this on every back boiler job. We work out the heat the room now needs. If the radiator is too small, we tell you and price a bigger one. Often a larger double panel radiator under the window does the job.</p>
      <div class="brx-note"><p><strong>Still have a back boiler?</strong> We take them out and fit a modern combi. See <a href="/boiler-installation-st-helens">boiler installation in St Helens</a>. We can also disconnect and cap the old gas fire safely.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="new-rooms">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Can you add a radiator to a room that has never had one?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Yes. A new radiator in a new position is from £325 including VAT. It usually takes 2 to 4 hours.</p>
      <p>Many St Helens terraces have changed over the years. A back bedroom once used for storage is now a bedroom. A dining room has been knocked through to the kitchen. A box room is now a home office. These rooms often have no radiator, or one that is far too small.</p>
      <p>We run new pipes from the nearest part of the circuit. Where we can, they go under the floorboards. Where we cannot, we box them in neatly. We check the boiler can heat the extra radiator first. Then we fit it with a TRV and balance the system.</p>
      <h3>Which radiator is right for me?</h3>
      <ul class="brx-list">
        <li><strong>Panel radiators.</strong> The most common type in St Helens. Double panels give the most heat for the money. This is what our £245 price covers.</li>
        <li><strong>Designer and vertical radiators.</strong> Good where wall space is tight. Many give less heat, so we check the output first.</li>
        <li><strong>Towel rails.</strong> In chrome, white or anthracite. A dual-fuel rail needs a safe electrical supply. Our partner firm <a href="https://www.idealelectricalsolutions.co.uk/">Ideal Electrical Solutions</a> can fit that.</li>
        <li><strong>TRVs.</strong> Set the heat in each room. £65 each, or up to six for £295. We leave one radiator without a TRV, often in the hall, so water can always flow.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="how">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How does a radiator installation work?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">A straight swap takes 1 to 2 hours. Five radiators are usually done in one day.</p>
      <ol class="sg-steps">
        <li><strong>Call for a price.</strong> A straight swap can often be priced on the phone. For front rooms, new rooms or new pipework, we visit and check the size and pipe route.</li>
        <li><strong>Fixed written price.</strong> It covers the radiator, fittings, labour and balancing. No add-ons on the day.</li>
        <li><strong>Drain and remove (30 minutes).</strong> We drain just that radiator where we can. If the valves will not hold, we drain the system.</li>
        <li><strong>Fit the new radiator (30 to 60 minutes).</strong> New brackets go up and the radiator is connected. Floors are covered.</li>
        <li><strong>Refill and balance (30 minutes).</strong> We top up the inhibitor, refill and bleed. Then we balance every radiator.</li>
        <li><strong>Old radiator taken away.</strong> We tidy up before we leave.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="brx-cta">
        <p><strong>Need new radiators in St Helens?</strong> Call for a fixed price, from £245 including VAT.</p>
        <a href={TEL} class="brx-btn">Call {PHONE}</a>
      </div>
      <h3>Should I power flush before fitting new radiators?</h3>
      <p>Older open-vented systems in WA10 often hold a lot of sludge. New radiators on a dirty system soon clog up.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>You need a flush first if</h3>
          <p>Several radiators are cold at the bottom. The water is brown or black when you bleed them. The boiler bangs or kettles. The heating is slow to warm up.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>You do not need one if</h3>
          <p>Every radiator heats evenly. The system warms up quickly. The water is clear when you bleed it. We just top up the inhibitor.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:1rem;">We check this when we price the job. A power flush is from £395. See <a href="/power-flushing-st-helens">power flushing in St Helens</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="repairs">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How much does a radiator repair cost in St Helens?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Repairs are charged by time. The first hour is £120 on weekdays from 9am to 4pm. There is no call-out fee.</p>
      <p>The first hour is £150 evenings, nights and weekends, and £180 on bank holidays. Most small repairs are done within it. If a job needs more time, we tell you the price before we carry on.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>Leaking valve.</strong> Often a loose gland nut or worn valve. In a terrace, a leak soon damages the floor and the ceiling below.</li>
        <li><strong>Stone cold.</strong> Often a stuck TRV pin or a closed valve. Usually a quick fix.</li>
        <li><strong>Cold at the bottom.</strong> Sludge has settled. Bleeding will not fix it. A flush will.</li>
        <li><strong>Rust or pinholes.</strong> The radiator is rusting from inside. It needs replacing, not repairing.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="brx-danger"><p><strong>Radiator leaking now?</strong> Put a bowl and towels under it. Turn both valves clockwise to close them. If it will not stop, turn the water off at the stopcock and call {PHONE}.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="st-helens">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Where in St Helens do you fit radiators?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Every St Helens postcode, WA9 to WA12. The price is the same wherever you live.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Postcodes</th><th>Typical homes</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Town centre, Eccleston</strong></td><td>WA10</td><td>Victorian terraces, many with old back boilers</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Parr, Sutton, Thatto Heath</strong></td><td>WA9</td><td>Older terraces, many back boiler swaps</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Haydock, Rainford</strong></td><td>WA11</td><td>Homes of mixed ages</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Newton-le-Willows, Earlestown</strong></td><td>WA12</td><td>Homes of mixed ages</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h3>Do you fit radiators for St Helens landlords?</h3>
      <p>Yes, at the same fixed prices. Many WA10 terraces are rented. When a radiator fails, your tenant needs heat back fast. We fit the right size radiator and balance the system. You get a written record of the work for your files. Need your yearly gas check too? See our <a href="/gas-safety-certificate-st-helens">gas safety certificates in St Helens</a>, from £75.</p>
      <p>Our heating engineers are part of our team led by James. All work on the heating circuit is done by our Gas Safe registered engineers. You can check any engineer on the <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk">Gas Safe Register</a>. We carry £2 million public liability insurance.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</ServiceGuide>
